# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Zahra — environment
# Copy to .env — every variable ships with a working local default except
# the tokens, which are only needed by the features that use them.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- Database (required: api + worker) ---
# Docker Compose exposes Postgres on 5433 to avoid clashing with a local install.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://zahra:zahra@localhost:5433/zahra

# --- Redis / BullMQ (required: api + worker) ---
# Docker Compose exposes Redis on 6380 for the same reason.
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6380

# --- API ---
API_PORT=3000

# --- GitHub PR channel (OPTIONAL — worker only) ---
# Needed ONLY to execute mutating actions through pull requests (fix_meta_tags…).
# Without it, Zahra still crawls, detects findings and proposes actions —
# execution of github_pr actions will just fail with a clear error.
#
# Use a FINE-GRAINED personal access token, scoped to the target site repo(s)
# only, with exactly two permissions: Contents (write) + Pull requests (write).
# GitHub App support is planned (PRs authored by a "zahra" identity instead of
# your personal account) — see docs/integration-github.md.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# --- Claude planner (OPTIONAL — worker only) ---
# With a key: the planner drafts complete actions (real title/metaDescription
# values, rationale, hypothesis) from the project digest.
# Without: deterministic rules planner — Zahra stays fully usable, you provide
# values via editedInput at approval. Also the automatic fallback on LLM errors.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ZAHRA_PLANNER_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-5

# --- Google Search Console (OPTIONAL — worker only) ---
# Service account JSON — see docs/integration-google.md for the 5-minute setup.
# Point to the key file, or inline the JSON (useful in containers):
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/path/to/zahra-sa.json
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=
